<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ashur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Assur was an ancient city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and the religious and original political capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>, named after its chief god. It remained the ceremonial centre of the Assyrian Empire even after the royal capital moved elsewhere. It was sacked by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> in 614 BCE during the fall of Assyria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assur.jpg" alt="Assur" width="320" height="173" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Véronique Dauge · CC BY-SA 3.0 igo · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ashur_(Qal%27at_Sherqat)-115188.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
